sue**: None\n\n**2. Save/Load Test** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Tests: Four test functions:\n  - `save_load_roundtrip()` (lines 7-26): Basic roundtrip serialization\n  - `save_load_with_source_water_catalog()` (lines 29-93): Catalog + process params persist\n  - `save_load_resume_determinism()` (lines 96-117): **240 + 480 = 720 hour test** - CORRECT\n  - `save_load_with_active_cycle_state()` (lines 120-155): Cycle state persistence\n- **Spec Requirement**: Save/load resume must yield 240 + 480 = 720 hours deterministic result\n- **Implementation**: Lines 96-108 correctly split at 240 hours, save, load, and resume for 480 more hours. Assertion at lines 110-114 validates full state equality.\n- **SaveFile Structure** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/save.rs, lines 11-17):\n  - `schema_version` (u32) ✓\n  - `app_version` (String) ✓\n  - `state` (TankState with full RNG state included) ✓\n  - `queued_actions` (Vec<PlayerAction>) ✓\n- **Issue**: None\n\n**3. Water Change Mass Balance Test** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/water_change_mass_balance.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Test: `water_change_50_percent_ro_like_halves_dissolved_totals()` (lines 15-115)\n- **Spec Requirement**: 50% water change with RO-like (zero nutrient) source should reduce dissolved totals by 50% ± 0.5%\n- **Implementation**: Lines 31-32 set tolerance = 0.005 (0.5%), expected_ratio = 0.5. Validates 12 different chemistry parameters (ammonia, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, Ca, Mg, Na, K, HCO3, Cl, SO4). Lines 101-112 properly check ratios within tolerance.\n- **Issue**: None\n\n**4. Tank Size & Thermal Response Test** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/tank_size_thermal_response.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Tests: Three test functions:\n  - `smaller_tank_responds_faster_to_ambient_change()` (lines 44-107): **10L vs 100L tank** with ambient change to 31°C. Validates 10L reaches half-delta **in fewer than half the ticks of 100L** (line 102-104 assertion). This captures the \"5x TAN peak\" and \"half thermal time\" requirements implicitly through volume scaling.\n  - `lid_slows_surface_heat_exchange()` (lines 110-137): Open vs closed lid geometry\n  - `feed_pulse_tan_concentration_scales_with_volume()` (lines 140-194): Feed pulse TAN concentration 10L vs 100L. **Line 189: asserts peak_tan_10l >= 5.0 * peak_tan_100l** - CORRECT (5x TAN peak requirement).\n- **Implementation**: Geometry correctly calculated for both tank sizes (lines 12-21). TAN mg/L properly tracked per volume.\n- **Issue**: None\n\n**5. Ambient Temperature Action Test** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/ambient_temperature_action.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Tests: Six test functions validating gradual temperature changes\n  - `ambient_change_causes_gradual_warming()` (lines 16-47): Changes ambient from 24°C to 31°C, validates:\n    - After 1 hour: water warmed but NOT jumped to 31°C (lines 26-35)\n    - After 200 hours: water near 31°C (lines 40-44)\n  - Other tests validate DO saturation decrease, heater behavior, etc.\n- **Spec Requirement**: Gradual rise (not instant)\n- **Implementation**: Correct, validates non-instantaneous response (lines 26-35).\n- **Issue**: None\n\n**6. Cycling Test (Seeded vs Unseeded)** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Test: `cycling_seeded_vs_unseeded()` (lines 13-96) and `filter_cleaning_setback()` (lines 99-146)\n- **Spec Requirement**: Seeded tank must stabilize earlier than unseeded tank during 30-day feed cycle\n- **Implementation**: \n  - Uses `tank_scenarios::cycling_fixture_pair(SimSeed(9000))` (line 14) which returns (seeded, unseeded) pair\n  - Seeded state (tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs, lines 727-738): AOB=0.20g, NOB=0.15g, comammox=0.05g, maturity=0.6\n  - Unseeded state (lines 743-754): AOB=0.005g, NOB=0.005g, comammox=0.001g, maturity=0.05\n  - Feeds 0.3g/day for 30 days (lines 31-58)\n  - Tracks stable hour (TAN < 0.1, NO2 < 0.1 after 48h)\n  - Lines 72-93: validates seeded stabilizes earlier or unseeded never stabilizes\n- **Issue**: None\n\n**7. Overfeeding Effects Test** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/overfeeding_effects.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Test: `overfeeding_effects()` (lines 4-53)\n- **Spec Requirement**: 14-day overfeeding (0.85g vs 0.18g) should increase detritus and lower DO\n- **Implementation**: \n  - 14-day loop (lines 14-31) with daily feeding and hourly stepping\n  - Control: 0.18g/day (line 15), Overfed: 0.85g/day (line 16)\n  - Validates detritus increase (lines 34-40)\n  - Validates nightly DO minimum lower in overfed (lines 41-44)\n  - Validates algae nuisance index higher (lines 45-50)\n- **Issue**: None\n\n**8. Rooted Substrate Advantage Test** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/rooted_substrate_advantage.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Test: `rooted_substrate_advantage()` (lines 55-81)\n- **Spec Requirement**: ActivePlanted substrate should give 15% biomass advantage at 30 days\n- **Implementation**:\n  - Compares RootFeedingRosette growth with ActivePlanted vs InertSand substrate (lines 56-63)\n  - Runs 30 days (24*30 hours, line 65-66)\n  - **Line 72-74: asserts active_biomass >= inert_biomass * 1.15** - CORRECT (15% advantage)\n  - Also validates nutrient depletion (lines 76-78)\n- **Issue**: None\n\n**9. Thermal Reproduction Penalty Test** (/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs)\n- **Status**: PASS\n- Test: `thermal_reproduction_penalty()` (lines 82-124)\n- **Spec Requirement**: 30°C tank should have 20% lower reproductive readiness than 25°C tank at 60 days\n- **Implementation**:\n  - Creates well-maintained 200L tank at 25°C and 30°C (lines 83-84, using `stocked_scenario()`)\n  - Runs 60 days with 0.1g/day feeding (lines 91-96)\n  - **Line 102-112: calculates readiness_reduction = 1.0 - (warm/cool), asserts >= 0.20** - CORRECT (20% penalty)\n  - Also validates fewer juveniles i